1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:09,610
Image to video. Colors look off.

2
00:00:09,610 --> 00:00:15,620
Four encodes, three readings.

3
00:00:15,620 --> 00:00:22,450
Source: red, green, blue, gray.

4
00:00:22,450 --> 00:00:32,020
Two readers: ffprobe tag, and decoded RGB.

5
00:00:32,020 --> 00:00:40,470
No tag. Pixels made with BT.601.

6
00:00:40,470 --> 00:00:50,330
Read as BT.709: green 255 becomes 215.

7
00:00:50,330 --> 00:00:56,190
BT.709 pixels plus a BT.709 tag: right.

8
00:00:56,190 --> 00:01:02,890
Read as BT.601: off by up to 23.

9
00:01:02,890 --> 00:01:14,490
6.1.1: no tag, read as 601, off by 23.

10
00:01:14,490 --> 00:01:23,520
8.1.2: FFmpeg writes the tag. Reads right.

11
00:01:23,520 --> 00:01:33,100
6.1.1: -colorspace only labels. Off by 40.

12
00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:41,310
8.1.2: it also converts. Reads right.

13
00:01:41,310 --> 00:01:44,750
Gray never moved. Colors do.

14
00:01:44,750 --> 00:01:49,560
Check the tag and the matrix together.
